+
+After booting up into Configuration Mode, a WOEEN is RECOMMENDED to send State Idle Notifications
+for all supported events in Configuration Mode to allow controllers to clear
+latched alarms. Without these State Idle Notifications, on controller side alarms could remain uncleared forever.
+
+In Self-Powered Mode the WOEEN Role Type will repeat sending its event(s) as long as it has energy.
+
+.. raw:: latex
+
+  \requirement{RT:10.12.0012.1}{0}
+
+It is RECOMMENDED to implement random delays between the repeated frames and
+with a minimum delay of 1 second, similar to the “ReportTime” as described in section
+:numref:`role_type_compliance_overview-security_bootstrapping-node_interview_response_timeouts`.
+
+.. raw:: latex
+
+  \requirement{RT:10.11.0013.1}{0}
+
+In any case, the WOEEN Role Type MUST NOT transmit repeated frames for more than 5 seconds,
+unless it pauses for at least 30 seconds, similar to the unsolicited bursts as described in
+:numref:`role_type_compliance_overview-unsolicited_communication-unsolicited_data_collection_communication`.
